  "term": "dentate gyrus",
  "definition": "The dentate gyrus is a region of gray matter located above the hippocampal gyrus. It has three layers, including a dense granule cell layer whose nerve fibers pass through the polymorphic layer and connect with pyramidal cell dendrites in the hippocampus.",
